{"id": "v200-u13-pull-unchecked", "matches": 1, "find": "    if(!base){ if(!_saveBusy) driveBaseSet(mySlug(), theirs); }\n    else if(theirs!==base){ driveClashSay(j, false); render(); }\n    return false;\n  }\n  if(DIRTY){\n    // UNSAVED WORK BEATS A NEWER FOLDER COPY. Adopting here would look exactly like the board\n    // losing what somebody had just typed.\n    setStat('⚠ <b>'+esc(j.by||'someone')+'</b> saved '+esc(APPN_LBL[mySlug()]||mySlug())\n      +' to the shared folder '+esc(liveAge(theirs))+', and you have unsaved changes. '\n      +'Nothing was replaced. Save yours, or reload to take theirs.');\n    render(); return false;\n  }\n  // THE EMPTY TEMPLATE HAS NO REQUIREMENTS UNTIL IT REOPENS. `DATA` is a const resolved at boot,\n  // so on the SHELL the folder's copy is persisted and the page reopened once - the same thing the\n  // routed import does. Only when the copy carries requirement data, or this would loop.\n  // A COPY WITH NO REQUIREMENT DATA IS NEVER ADOPTED, by any board. An empty template that saved\n  // before it had loaded anything would otherwise hand every full board a \"newer\" copy with nothing\n  // in it, and a board with no years cannot even draw itself. Nothing is changed here.\n  if(!_hasPack(j.store)){\n    setStat('⚠ The shared folder’s copy of '+esc(APPN_LBL[mySlug()]||mySlug())\n      +' carries no requirement data, so it was not loaded'\n      +(IS_SHELL? ', and this empty template cannot open it.' : ' — this board keeps its own.')\n      +' It needs to be saved once from a board that holds the requirements.');\n    render(); return false;\n  }\n  // v2.00 (U13, Brad 12 Oct): NOT WHILE A SAVE IS UNDER WAY -- checked here, after the last wait and before anything is\n  // changed, so a save that started while the folder was being read is seen too. A save that lands records the copy IT\n  // wrote as the one the work on screen came from, and marks the board saved: a copy loaded while it was writing stayed on\n  // screen recorded as saved, with the save's copy in the folder, and the next refresh and a reopen said nothing. Now\n  // nothing is changed -- what is on screen, the work kept aside and this browser's record stay exactly as they were -- and\n  // the next refresh once the save has finished decides afresh. A quiet refresh (the Live timer) says nothing, as it does\n  // when there is nothing newer; a Connect says so, in words that stay true once the save has landed. The words name this\n  // board's copy and nothing wider: the same Connect goes on to load the execution data, the reprogramming log and cost\n  // estimates from the folder. They name Load theirs as well, which runs in the same queue and counts here as a save does.\n  if(_saveBusy){\n    const lbl=esc(APPN_LBL[mySlug()]||mySlug())+' FY'+(MS.cur%100);\n    if(!quiet) setStat('⏳ The shared folder’s copy of '+lbl+' was <b>not loaded</b>", "repl": "    if(!base) driveBaseSet(mySlug(), theirs);\n    else if(theirs!==base){ driveClashSay(j, false); render(); }\n    return false;\n  }\n  if(DIRTY){\n    // UNSAVED WORK BEATS A NEWER FOLDER COPY. Adopting here would look exactly like the board\n    // losing what somebody had just typed.\n    setStat('⚠ <b>'+esc(j.by||'someone')+'</b> saved '+esc(APPN_LBL[mySlug()]||mySlug())\n      +' to the shared folder '+esc(liveAge(theirs))+', and you have unsaved changes. '\n      +'Nothing was replaced. Save yours, or reload to take theirs.');\n    render(); return false;\n  }\n  // THE EMPTY TEMPLATE HAS NO REQUIREMENTS UNTIL IT REOPENS. `DATA` is a const resolved at boot,\n  // so on the SHELL the folder's copy is persisted and the page reopened once - the same thing the\n  // routed import does. Only when the copy carries requirement data, or this would loop.\n  // A COPY WITH NO REQUIREMENT DATA IS NEVER ADOPTED, by any board. An empty template that saved\n  // before it had loaded anything would otherwise hand every full board a \"newer\" copy with nothing\n  // in it, and a board